      "writtenOn": "2019-05-31T22:15:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "address of 0 is reserved on the i2c bus for general call and it not valid for a specific device (it is also the value we get if no one sets it). I think it is a good signal that the i2c address is invalid and not available. It is 0 in the ITE tpcp_config_t case [0]\n\n\n[0] https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/06b2bd507f7b64267d4e73885c354c917a9dfa5b/baseboard/octopus/variant_usbc_ec_tcpcs.c",
      "parentUuid": "7df04ed5_d577e112",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "df6638d4f41ad3aad574213f6f3177cc308023c8",
